title: Outbound Spam via Direct SMTP
id: 20f03e87-ad17-4ed4-8957-569f899d73d2
status: experimental
description: Detects an internal, non-mail-server host making a large number of outbound SMTP (25/587) connections to many external servers, indicating a compromised host being used to send spam or phishing.
author: Alaris Global
references:
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1071/003/
logsource:
  category: firewall
detection:
  selection:
    dst_port:
      - 25
      - 587
    direction: 'outbound'
  timeframe: 10m
  condition: selection | count(dst_ip) by src_ip > 50
  condition: selection
fields:
  - src_ip
  - dst_ip
  - dst_port
falsepositives:
  - Authorized mail relays
level: medium
tags:
  - attack.command_and_control
  - attack.t1071.003
